    'home.problem.title': 'In MT5, the #1 result is often the most fragile',
    'home.problem.mt5.kicker': 'What MT5 gives you (example)',
    'home.problem.mt5.pick': 'MT5’s #1: Pass 1842',
    'home.problem.mt5.note': 'The highest Result among thousands of passes',
    'home.problem.mt5.body': 'MT5 sorts configurations by the criterion you chose. With thousands tested, the ones at the top are often the least reliable: change one parameter a single step and they can fall apart.',
    'home.problem.oro.kicker': 'What Orometra does',
    'home.problem.oro.pick': 'Recommended: Pass 4283',
    'home.problem.oro.note': '#1 rejected: isolated peak',
    'home.problem.oro.body': 'It looks for zones where neighboring values also work — a plateau. That is harder to get by chance, so it tends to hold up better.',
    'home.problem.fig.aria': 'Example: MT5’s #1 is an isolated peak whose neighbors miss your minimums; Orometra picks the center of a plateau where they all clear them.',
    'home.problem.fig.floor': 'YOUR MINIMUMS',
    'home.problem.fig.peak': 'MT5 #1 · 1842',
    'home.problem.fig.pick': 'Pass 4283',
    'home.engine.sub': 'What would take you hours in a spreadsheet and a lot of judgment — done in seconds, the same way every time.',
    'home.engine.1.title': 'Drops what doesn\'t qualify',
    'home.engine.1.body': 'Out go the passes that miss your minimums for profit, drawdown and trades.',
    'home.engine.2.title': 'Doesn\'t trust the Result column',
    'home.engine.2.body': 'It measures quality with objective metrics, not with what you optimized for.',
    'home.engine.3.title': 'Checks the neighbors',
    'home.engine.3.body': 'Inside the plateau it picks what holds in both periods alongside its neighbors, not the peak.',
    'home.engine.4.title': 'Checks it against the forward',
