    'home.ai.more': 'Read the full explanation →',
    'home.how.1.title': 'Export',
    'home.how.1.body': 'Export your MT5 optimization results to XML — and the forward tab, if you used it.',
    'home.how.2.title': 'Drop them here',
    'home.how.2.body': 'They are analyzed in your browser, in seconds.',
    'home.how.3.title': 'Take away your configuration',
    'home.how.3.body': 'The recommended one with its reasons, how reliable it is, a .set ready for MT5 and the range to re-optimize around it.',
    'home.faq.title': 'Frequently asked questions',
    'home.faq.1.q': 'Which files do I need?',
    'home.faq.1.a': 'The XML that MT5 exports with your optimization results: right-click the table and export to XML. If you enabled forward, export that table too. The .opt file does not work. <a href="/guides/export-mt5-optimization-xml/">Step-by-step guide</a>.',
    'home.faq.2.q': 'What if I did not enable forward?',
    'home.faq.2.a': 'You can still analyze it, but the evidence will not go beyond “weak”: without data the optimization never saw, a robust plateau cannot be told apart from a lucky one. Next time, enable it in the tester settings (a quarter or a third of the period).',
    'home.faq.3.q': 'Does it work with genetic optimization?',
    'home.faq.3.a': 'Yes. Since the genetic algorithm does not test every combination, plateaus are measured conservatively: the result may fall short, but it never invents support. The report tells you.',
    'home.faq.5.q': 'Does it work with my EA?',
    'home.faq.5.a': 'With any MetaTrader 5 EA, on any symbol and timeframe: Orometra does not read your code, only the results table. MetaTrader 4 is not supported for now.',
    'home.faq.4.q': 'What happens to my data?',
    'home.faq.4.a': 'Nothing leaves your computer: the analysis runs in your browser. We only count, anonymously, visits and how often each feature is used. Details in the <a href="privacy/">privacy page</a>.',
    'home.faq.6.q': 'Will it tell me whether my EA will make money?',
    'home.faq.6.a': 'No. It tells you how much your data supports the chosen configuration; no level means “trade it”. It does not predict the market or turn a weak EA into a good one, and if your backtest is optimistic (spread, history quality), so is the analysis.',
    'home.faq.7.q': 'Why not just ask an AI?',
    'home.faq.7.a': 'It will give you a convincing explanation, different every time. Orometra is a fixed calculation: same files, same result; it knows how to say “insufficient”, and your parameters never leave your computer. <a href="/methodology/#ia">Full comparison</a>.',
    'home.final.title': 'Ready to try it?',
    'home.final.body': 'Drop your optimization here and see it in a minute. Nothing is uploaded.',
